<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43716" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">seps</span></b> , sēpis,
		comm., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σήψ</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A venomous serpent</i>, <i>whose bite
				occasioned putrefaction</i>, <i><span class="en">Luc. 9,
				764 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9,
				723</span></i>.—<i>Acc. sing.</i> sepa,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				29, 5, 32, § 102</span></i>.—<i>Acc.
				Plur.</i> sepas, <i><span class="en">Plin. 23, 2, 29, § 61</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Tert. Carm. adv. Marc. 1, 1 <i>fin.</i></span></i>; <i><span class="en">Aus.
				Idyll. Grammat. 12, 14</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>An insect</i>, perh. <i>the
			wood-louse</i>, <i>milleped</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 20, 2,
				6, § 12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">29, 6, 39, §
			137</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
